==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} ''[[#Old Norse|þeir]]''.

===Pronoun===
'''þeir''' {{m}}

# {{sense|personal pronoun}} {{nominative}} ''plural'' of the word ''[[hann#Icelandic|hann]]'' meaning "[[he]]"; literally meaning "[[they]]"
#* ''[[hvernig|Hvernig]] [[vita]] '''þeir''' [[þetta]]?''
#*: [[how|How]] [[do]] '''they''' [[know]] [[that]]?''
#* ''[[strákur|Strákar]]; '''þeir''' [[elska]] [[stelpa|stelpur]] [[og]] [[stelpa|stelpur]] [[elska]] [[þá]].
#*: [[boy|Boys]]; '''they''' [[love]] [[girl]]s [[and]] [[girl]]s [[love]] [[them]].
# {{sense|demonstrative pronoun}}, ''plural'' of {{term|sá|lang=non}}

